<article class="env-lemma" id="03WK">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03WK">Lemma <span data-tag="03WK">67.21.1</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $f : X \to Y$ be a representable morphism of algebraic spaces over $S$. Then $f$ is quasi-affine (in the sense of Section <a href="/tag/03HA" data-tag="03HA">67.3</a>) if and only if for all affine schemes $Z$ and morphisms $Z \to Y$ the scheme $X \times _ Y Z$ is quasi-affine. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This follows directly from the definition of a quasi-affine morphism of schemes (Morphisms, Definition <a href="/tag/01SK" data-tag="01SK">29.13.1</a>). 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>